# [All comparisons](/comparison/)

This page compares zanity with [mockbuster](https://github.com/benomahony/mockbuster) on the same source files.
Generated by `bench/parity/parity.py` on 2026-10-17, against zanity `7c4a2e5`.

# Rule by rule

Same line means zanity reports it on the tool's line, give or take one. A note identifies deliberate differences.

| Its rule | zanity rule | It fires | zanity fires | Same line | Note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `mock-instantiation` | `test-double` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `mocker-fixture` | `test-double` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✗ no]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) | [✗ no]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) | zanity reports the double where it is made, such as mocker.patch, not the parameter |
| `monkeypatch-fixture` | `test-double` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✗ no]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) | [✗ no]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) | zanity reports monkeypatch.setattr, which replaces behaviour, not setenv or the parameter |
| `patch-call` | `test-double` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `patch-context` | `test-double` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `patch-decorator` | `test-double` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |

# Real code

## Recall

Of each tool's findings, how many zanity reports on the same lines with a mapped rule.

| Tool | Its rule | zanity rule | Note | Its findings | zanity too | Recall |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| mockbuster | `monkeypatch-fixture` | `test-double` | zanity reports monkeypatch.setattr, which replaces behaviour, not setenv or the parameter | 14 | 0 | [0%]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) |

## Agreement

Of zanity's findings, how many the tool also reports. Low agreement is zanity finding what the tool doesn't, which can be either tool's mistake.

| Tool | zanity rule | zanity findings | Tool too | Agreement |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| mockbuster | `test-double` | 16 | 0 | 0% |
